# Behavioural coverage row 12 "Multiple cities": found a second, independent city of the same
# realm on a NON-adjacent surface parasang, refuse a further founding on ground now held, and
# prove the seat comes back when the founder returns to the first city.
#
# City one is founded by the built-in realize verb -- the production first-city transaction,
# never a harness copy. City two is founded through KingdomFounding.FoundSecond
# (Core/KingdomFounding.03.SiteJudgmentAndStyle.cs:69), the same transaction the founder's
# basin rite commits through, with Force FALSE so the adjacency law stands.
#
# SYNTHETIC SETUP, DISCLOSED:
#  - the founder is relocated with zero-energy SystemMoveTo plus SetActiveZone, not walked
#    across the world map; travel time, encounters and the away economy are NOT exercised.
#  - FoundSecond is the waterless route: the rite's 8-dram debit and its three Popup prompts
#    (name, vocation, refusal) are NOT exercised. A sealed script cannot answer a popup, and
#    Harness/KingdomScenarioVerbProvider.cs forbids a provider from showing one.
#  - the second site is ordinary worldgen; only the START zone is born-clean. The site is
#    accepted only if it builds, answers to no foreign faction, offers an empty landing cell
#    and reads Allowed from KingdomFounding.JudgeSite. Every rejected candidate is journalled.
#  - city two has no population, buildings, stockpile or economy, and no turn is spent: every
#    case re-proves Game.Turns and Game.TimeTicks are unchanged.
#
# NOT COVERED, DISCLOSED: save -> cold load -> next action on either city (row 12's
# save_cold_load sub-scope stays a gap), the third city and the RealmIsFull cap, and ordinary
# pedestrian travel between the two cities.
#
# The return leg asserts production's own seat exchange: KingdomSystem.HandleEvent
# (ZoneActivatedEvent) calls TrySeat before the claim guard (Core/KingdomSystem.z20.Events.cs),
# so activating the first city's ground must bring its seat back with nothing seated here.
DESCRIPTION=a realm founds a second city on a non-adjacent parasang, refuses a further founding on its own ground, and recovers the first city's seat on return
REQUEST=founding-first-city
START=8.22@40,12
SCRIPT=stagedigest;realize;second-city-setup;second-city-check;second-city-check;second-city-check;second-city-check;stagedigest
VERBS=second-city-setup,second-city-check
EXPECT=stagedigest:OK~founded=false,realize:OK,second-city-site:OK~adjacent=false,second-city-setup:OK~cases=4 passed=0 failed=0,second-city-check:OK~case=travel-out,second-city-topology:OK~settlements=2,second-city-check:OK~case=found-second,second-city-check:OK~case=refused-already-ours,second-city-check:OK~cases=4 passed=4 failed=0,stagedigest:OK~founded=true,COMPLETE
SET=founding,growth,native-regression
TIMEOUT=900
